  "term": "noetic",
  "definition": "Noetic refers to what belongs to thought or reason rather than to the senses. In a stricter philosophical use, it means ideas taken to arise directly from reason itself, while in a broader use it means ideas considered apart from sensory reference; it can also describe mental processes that involve cognition.",
